<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">If this is to be the end for Cristiano Ron=
aldo at international level, at least it can be said that he left the stage=
 as he bestrode it: with monumental self-regard. Ronaldo has always been a =
preening, self-absorbed player, but for a time, when he was one of the best=
 in the world, it could be tolerated. For the past four years, though, he h=
as actively and obviously held Portugal back. There is a great generation o=
f technical talent here weighed down by the monstrous albatross of his ego.=
</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">To recap the basic details of the past cou=
ple of weeks. Ronaldo played 67 minutes of <a href=3D"https://ablink.editor=
ial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgt=
jhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgqFWXop7RbVUzAvoJXLjJe3B0OebRZdnGsJoriBN-WJkIALI468FAcKUr=
XzHCORP6StzjYaN8XxqjnCCPyBDwz5DXef8paqtNGWKG0YTLe7c5jYgM1ehIEQvgEWug9kVAsmK=
s4Prw37G_rAhVnPxfInMY0LStVZr8tD7VisDCfUq7lU-VCjxq_Im0K5L3zJVRxxe-00ajjpEFqX=
tmoVXVbNNmosGAaU2OsYIfo2RAMv5Jq9WRnXcZeMF4GDCZ9glJ1_5hqMVeEiofEkUt87QHYA/4u=
m/ybKYpe5tRGKFM-p7Y7JPYA/h21/h001.aUwY3289wgmC3J3l6btFAC8c4A-feD573RpTPVJz5=
sE" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Portugal=E2=80=99s scratchy 1-0 win over Wale=
s</a>. Portugal coach Jorge Jesus, who replaced Roberto Mart=C3=ADnez after=
 the World Cup, said he had a verbal agreement with Ronaldo that he would n=
ot start the following game against Norway but would perhaps come off the b=
ench. Early in the second half, Ronaldo went to warm up =E2=80=93 although =
whether that was on his own initiative or because Jesus had told him to is =
unclear. The game was tight, Portugal ultimately winning 2-1, and Jesus did=
 not bring Ronaldo on.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">To Ronaldo and his army of apologists, Jes=
us was guilty of an unacceptable provocation. Jesus=E2=80=99s view was that=
 winning the game took priority over the extremely delicate feelings of a 4=
1-year-old forward. <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/=
c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgDfKe=
_6xbwlUhh-I9v_HW3KrHY_yP44TC0vknXQ2OSreiRvL-G7MuUJPiZjnas76Evoue9qV_1_S0smQ=
D5-p96UhrUis5h9pehdb3KGYWOkHF-ZYRVHK1DfZVseSwVu9QhulD6O2IozOfAwRaxwEXA5n8a1=
Pvm6n98OxZvYlEVdPeTZnOofdzIca8RvYU6ltIFEKKK_8otvBpHOnJULu65Xp7CjzXdEzyW8GrP=
bINGRjE7jXmMS4RAAOECrPxxPqFd5WcCi_0NhQFE2Bb3MtbzO90EQS0UtDgunICwGDBjZNqF7of=
Gj9Qij9KRYp9kmMP/4um/ybKYpe5tRGKFM-p7Y7JPYA/h22/h001.ND4bTEEFTptot0wQpaOCtB=
nMSX3eL2tSNYbJbF6e00Q" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Ronaldo walked out on the =
squad</a>, and perhaps on his international career, although only three day=
s later, seemingly after Jesus had refused to pay penance for his blasphemy=
. Which is sad, although perhaps not quite in the way Ronaldo thinks it is.=
</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It=E2=80=99s possible Jesus, who also coac=
hed Ronaldo at Al Nassr, could have handled the situation differently. He i=
s not, it=E2=80=99s fair to say, a diplomat. After Mart=C3=ADnez=E2=80=99s =
soft-pedalling, that is, though, perhaps exactly what was needed. Jesus is =
72. His vision of management is old-school, which is to say that he is a di=
ctator and he takes orders only from the club president, and then only if h=
e feels like it. His career has been characterized by rifts with players wh=
o have resisted him. In a sense the only surprise is that his falling out w=
ith Ronaldo took until the second game of his reign.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Others might have been cowed in the face o=
f Ronaldo=E2=80=99s sulk, the online backlash and criticism from some of th=
e Portuguese press, certain elements of which Ronaldo owns, but not Jesus. =
He is a man of great eloquence and is always quotable but, even by his stan=
dards, his response to the furore has been remarkable as he has insisted on=
 the primacy of the team over any individual. =E2=80=9CI can say to any pla=
yer that you=E2=80=99re starting on the bench: if I need you for 30 minutes=
 you=E2=80=99re going to play, if I don=E2=80=99t need you, you=E2=80=99re =
not going to play,=E2=80=9D he said. =E2=80=9CThe way I was reading the gam=
e he didn=E2=80=99t come on. Because it=E2=80=99s not Cristiano, just like =
it will never be any player that will change my ideas as the coach. Never! =
Not him, not anyone in football. Not him, not anyone, not any president. Ne=
ver! Zero!=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">His hardline approach might have backfired=
 had Portugal then lost to Denmark, but they won 4-2, playing superbly. Gon=
=C3=A7alo Ramos, who might have thought he had already settled this argumen=
t by replacing Ronaldo at the 2022 World Cup for the last-16 game against S=
witzerland and <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u00=
1.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEAL7GJWVk6OP-hWZy2kpgSEomXElvCV8=
ClSKcOpRnZakEsY_zEVMgnyZDDiyYIhjsyET-X3n0UPmiSMWRRbHj3r7h0TT5s2CFjoYGu44EwL=
K8T_rWl_b7dIAdquEETeGMj9Zfzy2JHlJ1V3MnujHLNtLibbPQiKogARER6NByG5slzvjuyzfk3=
193pv5VfrRg_iAO6dG0PsMQ26SNODz5zLXBjbaECU-60oRUfO6jAiU4X6OH4_TwVvswYAC67EaD=
t1Q7XwWd67TeMDBImaStWLafS_9eV9PDRiCd4gpd0P0A/4um/ybKYpe5tRGKFM-p7Y7JPYA/h23=
/h001.LBsitQdztOyhMeSaaRGdwkHBX6CM8l8zJ_8uc_EPbhw" style=3D"color: #0077B6;=
">scoring a hat-trick in a 6-1 win</a>, set up the first and scored another=
 against the Danes, having already scored the winner against Norway. =E2=80=
=9CThe new manager is a great help,=E2=80=9D Ramos said. =E2=80=9CWe have c=
learer ideas; we know exactly where each teammate is, both in defense and a=
ttack. We=E2=80=99re improving day by day, and it=E2=80=99s all part of a p=
rocess. We=E2=80=99re very happy with the win, once again against a good te=
am.=E2=80=9D Ramos was on target Sunday as Portugal came from behind to bea=
t Norway at home, making it four wins out of four in this window.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The tendency until now has been for the ot=
her Portugal players to back Ronaldo, to insist he was an icon and that the=
y didn=E2=80=99t mind his superannuated lumbering. Bruno Fernandes has been=
 notably diplomatic, but others are starting to break cover. Ramos=E2=80=99=
s former Paris Saint-Germain teammate Vitinha, for instance, who has seen a=
t club level how beneficial a purge of egos can be, observed that Portugal=
=E2=80=99s improvement has been =E2=80=9Cthe work of the coach =E2=80=A6 I =
think beyond the win, the content of our game was great.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Jesus has offered Ronaldo another meeting =
to try to resolve the situation, but the Portuguese football federation see=
ms already to have accepted how the affair will end, beginning plans for a =
farewell game for the country=E2=80=99s record scorer. Both Jesus and Ronal=
do have indicated they will say more this week.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">But the truth is that this is a break that=
 should have happened long ago. For three tournaments, Ronaldo has undermin=
ed an extremely talented Portugal. This is a sad story. It is sad Ronaldo=
=E2=80=99s career should have ended this way. But the saddest element is th=
at a great player could be so deluded about his own fading ability that a n=
ational team=E2=80=99s hopes and dreams should have been sacrificed to his =
quest to break goalscoring records.</p>
