<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>By Jeff Rueter</strong></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">From the outside, a moment like the one Ca=
van Sullivan produced Saturday seemed to be pulled directly from dreamland.=
 Turns out, it pretty much was.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CI was amazed. I was excited,=E2=
=80=9D the 17-year-old said of learning he=E2=80=99d start for the US men=
=E2=80=99s national team against Mexico, in what would become a 3-0 win. =
=E2=80=9CI texted my family right after, and after lunch, I took a nap. Bef=
ore I go to sleep, I visualize and try to manifest good things for the nigh=
t. Some things come to fruition, some don=E2=80=99t.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Sullivan visualized scoring, and celebrati=
ng with a knee slide towards the corner. Hours later, he was doing exactly =
that, picking off a poor pass from goalkeeper Ra=C3=BAl Rangel and chipping=
 him from 35 yards out to become the USMNT=E2=80=99s youngest-ever goalscor=
er, sliding toward the corner flag with his teammates in hot pursuit.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CThat wasn=E2=80=99t the way I pic=
tured scoring a goal, but the celebration was,=E2=80=9D Sullivan said.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.thegua=
